# Thread `PRRT_kwDOTXdlLc6yY6hJ` — IMPORTANT: failed mint leaves the orphan tag pushed (release_tag_mint.sh:98)

**Fixed** — the mint rolls the untrained tag back before failing, so the prescribed "fix the credential and re-run" actually re-mints instead of silently re-arming the stranded-draft shape.

`scripts/release_tag_mint.sh` (verification-failure branch):

- `::warning::rolling back the untrained tag ref so a fixed re-run can re-mint`, then `git push <token-URL> ":refs/tags/$tag"`;
- if the rollback itself fails: `::warning::rollback of refs/tags/$tag failed — a re-run will skip the mint (tag exists) and can strand the draft; delete refs/tags/$tag manually before re-running` (the failure is named, never silent);
- the **local** tag object is dropped too (`git tag -d`) — your reproduction's reused-workspace `fatal: tag already exists` at `git tag -a` on a self-hosted re-run is covered;
- then the loud `::error::tag train did not start …` and exit 1.

The late-train race you flagged as acceptable is accepted as-is (same pushed-before-failure window as today).

**Behavioral test**: `test/release_tag_mint_test.dart`, "a failed train verification rolls the pushed tag back so a fixed re-run re-mints" — attempt 1 (`GH_STUB_TRAIN_RUNNING=0`) asserts the error + the rollback warning, `ls-remote --exit-code` rc 2 on the bare origin (ref gone), and an empty `git tag -l` in the work clone (local object gone); attempt 2 on a fresh minter with the train visible then **re-mints end-to-end (exit 0)** — exactly the recovery path the orphan tag used to break. The two caller-suite silent-train tests (`release_attach_or_create_mint_test.dart`, `release_lazy_draft_mint_test.dart`) now also assert the rollback delete-push was captured next to the mint push.
